Certainly! Below is a simple HTML template that you can use to create a basic webpage. This template includes a header, a main content area, and a footer. You can customize it further based on your specific needs.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Webpage</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
        }
        header {
            background-color: #333;
            color: #fff;
            padding: 10px 0;
            text-align: center;
        }
        main {
            padding: 20px;
        }
        footer {
            background-color: #333;
            color: #fff;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 10px 0;
            position: fixed;
            width: 100%;
            bottom: 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to My Webpage</h1>
    </header>
    <main>
        <h2>Here is some content.</h2>
        <p>This is some sample text that will be displayed on the page.</p>
    </main>
    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2023 My Webpage. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: The HTML structure includes a `<head>` section with meta tags for character set, viewport settings, and a title. The `<body>` section contains the main content area.
- **Header**: The header is styled with a background color, text color, padding, and alignment.
- **Main Content Area**: The main content area is styled with padding and a background color.
- **Footer**: The footer is styled with a background color, text color, padding, and alignment.

You can customize the content, styles, and layout as needed to fit your specific requirements.
